the target language is: prolog.

the functions are:
    the household income is *a number*.
    the income limit of the parameters is *a number*.
    the household income limit is *a truth value*.

the knowledge base household_income_limit includes:

the text of the_model is at "sources/P-5bdf1ac7-b0ca-403b-89f9-7f1504f6bf26-1.0.0.dmn".

% Passes when yearly household income is at or below incomeLimit. Each benefit that uses this check sets its own incomeLimit; Philly Cash uses 40000. A blank income gives Need more information.
rule household_income_limit_1 with provenance the model at decision Household income limit:
the household income limit is true if
    it is not the case that
        it is not the case that the household income is a number
        or it is not the case that the income limit of the parameters is a second number
    and the household income is a number N
    and the income limit of the parameters is a number M
    and N <= M.

rule household_income_limit_2 with provenance the model at decision Household income limit:
the household income limit is false if
    it is not the case that
        it is not the case that the household income is a number
        or it is not the case that the income limit of the parameters is a second number
    and the household income is a number N
    and the income limit of the parameters is a number M
    and N > M.

